            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: what did nakhaṁ mean, and what did ellŭ mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: കൂടുതൽ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കൂടുതൽ (kūṭutal) — \"more\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Built on കൂടുക (kūṭuka), \"to join, to gather, to increase\", with a tail Malayalam puts on a doing to turn it into a thing. The whole says, roughly, \"an increasing\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It answers the question at a Kerala meal, where a server comes round the leaf a second and a third time and the guest has to say something. കൂടുതൽ (kūṭutal) asks for more."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The long ū at the front carries the word. Shorten it and you have said something else entirely, so it is worth stretching."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five short answers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
