        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: കുറവ്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കുറവ് (kuṟavŭ) — \"less, a shortage\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The mirror of the last one, built the same way: കുറയുക (kuṟayuka), \"to lessen, to fall short\", plus a tail that makes the doing into a thing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കുറവ് (kuṟavŭ) is less of something, and it is also a shortfall or a lack. A house short of water has a water കുറവ് (kuṟavŭ), and a piece of work with something missing has a കുറവ് (kuṟavŭ) in it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The റ here is the hard trilled one you met in the rock-word, and the ŭ closes the word the way it closed the root-word and the seed-word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two, and they are opposites built from the same parts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
