        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: പോരും",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പോരും (pōruṁ) — \"that will do, that is enough\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From പോരുക (pōruka), \"to suffice\", and it means that what is there is already enough."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Set it against mati, which you already have. The two overlap, and either will stop a server; പോരും (pōruṁ) leans a little more towards \"that reaches far enough\" and mati towards \"stop\". Kerala uses both, often in the same breath."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ം at the end is the anusvara, the humming close you have met on the sky-word and the star-word and the vessel-word. It closes a great many Malayalam words, and by now it should be arriving without thought."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five, and you can answer a served plate five ways: more, less, a little, no need, that will do."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
